WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.549 --> 00:00:03.179
It turns out, all our teachers were wrong.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:09.500
The correct way to count is 4, 5, 6, 1, 2,
3, 7, 8, 9 well, at least from a certain point

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.200
of view.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.700
Star Wars is known today as a cultural phenomenon,
but it wasn't always seen that way.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:19.940
The original film, A New Hope, was released
back in 1977 with little hope of success by

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.840
even its creator, George Lucas.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.440
According to Screen Prism, Lucas was so sure
of its failure that when it was released in

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.140
cinemas, he was hiding out in Hawaii on vacation.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.880
But Lucas must have had some belief that the
movie could be a hit, because buried deep

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:37.440
in his mind was a plan to turn what looked
like a standalone film into a series of movies.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.510
And then, something incredible happened.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.580
"If you strike me down, I shall become more
powerful than you could possibly imagine."

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.340
A New Hope then simply titled Star Wars defied
the odds and became a mega hit of galactic

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.100
proportions.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.980
A New Hope was followed by The Empire Strikes
Back in 1980, and Return of the Jedi came

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:59.430
after in 1983 to complete the original Star
Wars trilogy.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:03.179
Then, in 1999, a fourth Star Wars film was
released.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.680
Only, it wasn't a fourth film it was to be
the first one on the Star Wars timeline.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.100
The Phantom Menace is in fact episode 1.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.980
It was succeeded by episode 2, Attack of the
Clones, in 2002, and episode 3, Revenge of

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.760
the Sith, in 2005, to comprise a Star Wars
prequel trilogy.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:24.940
More films were released from 2015 to 2019
The Force Awakens, The Last Jedi, and The

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:29.380
Rise of Skywalker which were sequels to the
original three Star Wars films.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.120
But why create them in this order?

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:36.640
Why not make the first Star Wars trilogy prequels,
then create two separate sequel collections?

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:40.440
The answer is a lot simpler than its accompanying
questions suggest.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:45.380
Author Michael Kaminski writes in The Secret
History of Star Wars that Lucas decided to

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:50.460
start with the fourth episode quote, "due
to technical and storytelling reasons."

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.700
He further explained:

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:56.740
"Lucas had a massive, expensive epic on his
hands, and divided the story into three separate

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.240
films.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.480
He had also developed a backstory for his
elaborate tale, which together totaled six

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:07.520
chapters, and sought to make Episode IV first,
due to technical and storytelling reasons.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.940
When the film by some miracle went into production,
it was beset by problems of all kinds, and

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.750
Lucas was sure it would be a failure and was
shocked when it became the biggest sensation

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:17.240
of the year."

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.380
Lucas himself has corroborated this claim.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.220
He admitted:

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.660
"The Star Wars series started out as a movie
that ended up being so big that I took each

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:31.160
act and cut it into its own movie [...] When
I first did Star Wars, I did it as a big piece.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.940
It was like a big script.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.900
It was way too big to make into a movie.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:39.240
So I took the first third of it, which is
basically the first act, and I turned that

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.180
into what was the original Star Wars."

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:46.300
The story of A New Hope gave no context of
the world in the film, throwing viewers straight

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:48.910
into the action without any background knowledge.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:53.431
Doing so would later give Lucas the opportunity
to go back and provide some context in the

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.060
prequels.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.620
From the release of the first Star Wars film,
there was talk that Lucas had three trilogies

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:02.990
in mind one of which would be a prequel trilogy
that would deal with the political background

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:06.870
needed for the Empire to become what it was
in the original movie.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.380
Lucas always knew he wanted to create an entire
galaxy far, far away not just a standalone

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:11.880
film.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.031
There's plenty of evidence of that in A New
Hope, with references to the Clone Wars, the

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.460
Jedi Order, and the Kessel Run hinting at
an untold history.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.810
It took a number of different drafts of the
first Star Wars film before the story of Luke

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:29.040
Skywalker, a poor farm boy from Tattoine who
discovers he has Jedi powers and joins a band

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.840
of rebels against an evil dictatorship in
the form of the Empire, took shape leaving

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.530
other characters by the wayside to have their
stories told later.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:41.330
Lucas kept them in the bank, and put some
of his ideas into the film in passing mention

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.360
to give that backstory.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:47.360
Mace Windy — who became Mace Windu 
in the final story — and Annikin Starkiller,

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.530
later Anakin Skywalker, are among
the characters who were initially meant to

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.080
be in the first film in Lucas' early drafts.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.460
Both appear in the Star Wars prequels, although
Anakin was technically part of the original

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.580
trilogy given that he eventually transforms
into Darth Vader.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:06.180
Lucas had a pretty specific vision in mind
for A New Hope: he wanted the film to fade

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:10.800
in with audiences, making it feel like they
were coming in halfway through a larger story.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.080
It would pave the way for Lucas to be able
to turn the film into a full movie series,

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.720
and he already had groundwork laid for the
backstory he would need to tell.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:23.840
"But what about the final trilogy of the Skywalker
Saga headlined by the powerful, young Rey?"

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:24.720
you might be wondering.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:29.960
Though Lucas already had it set in his mind
to make episodes 7 through 9 way back when,

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.200
he hadn't yet mapped the actual story that
would unfold in those three films.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.800
What he did know was that he wanted the original
three heroes to make a return, according to

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.780
ComicBook.com.

00:04:39.949 --> 00:04:43.879
Lucas got his wish on that final point giving
them a chance to say their final goodbyes

00:04:43.879 --> 00:04:49.050
as the Skywalker saga comes to an end with
the release of The Rise of Skywalker on December

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:49.540
20.

